{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-46452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Factor $2{y}^{2}-8y+26.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we let $f(y)=2{y}^{2}-8y+26.$\n\nNext, we solve $f(y)=0$ by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y) & =0 \\\\ 2{y}^{2}-8y+26 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-4y+13 & =0 \\\\ ({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot y+{2}^{2})-{2}^{2}+13 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-4+13 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =-9 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =9{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & ={(3\\text{i})}^{2} \\\\ y-2 & =\\pm 3\\text{i} \\\\ y & =2\\pm 3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since our quadratic equation has roots ${y}_{1}=2+3\\text{i}$ and ${y}_{2}=2-3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ the expression $2{y}^{2}-8y+26$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-8y+26 & =a(y-{y}_{1})(y-{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =2(y-(2+3\\text{i}))(y-(2-3\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2f3b35cd8b358cc9172c7517507c82854978f7cf090f8872c2b39fc9fe496f7a"} {"question" "q-46452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(y-(1+3\\text{i}))(y-(1-3\\text{i}))"] ["math" "(y-(2+3\\text{i}))(y-(2-3\\text{i}))"] ["math" "2(y-(1+3\\text{i}))(y-(1-3\\text{i}))"] ["math" "2(y-(2+3\\text{i}))(y-(2-3\\text{i}))"] ["math" "2(y-(2+\\text{i}))(y-(2-\\text{i}))"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2(y-(2+3\\text{i}))(y-(2-3\\text{i}))"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quadratic polynomial $P(y)$ has the double root ${y}_{1}={y}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3.$ Find $P(y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root ${y}_{1}={y}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(y-{y}_{1})^{2} & =3{(y-3)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{(y-3)}^{2} & =3({y}^{2}-6y+9) \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}-18y+27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(y)=3{y}^{2}-18y+27.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2f3b35cd8b358cc9172c7517507c82854978f7cf090f8872c2b39fc9fe496f7a"} {"question" "q-46588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{y}^{2}-18y+27"] ["math" "3{y}^{2}-18y-27"] ["math" "3{y}^{2}-24y+27"] ["math" "3{y}^{2}-9y+27"] ["math" "3{y}^{2}-9y-27"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3{y}^{2}-18y+27"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46657" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is a factor of ${u}^{2}-4u+40?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46657" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we let $f(u)={u}^{2}-4u+40.$\n\nNext, we solve $f(u)=0$ by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(u) & =0 \\\\ {u}^{2}-4u+40 & =0 \\\\ ({u}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot u+{2}^{2})-{2}^{2}+40 & =0 \\\\ (u-2)^{2}-4+40 & =0 \\\\ (u-2)^{2}+36 & =0 \\\\ (u-2)^{2} & =-36 \\\\ (u-2)^{2} & =36{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ (u-2)^{2} & =(6\\text{i})^{2} \\\\ u-2 & =\\pm 6\\text{i} \\\\ u & =2\\pm 6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our quadratic equation has roots ${u}_{1}=2+6\\text{i}$ and ${u}_{2}=2-6\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1,$ the expression ${u}^{2}-4u+40$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-4u+40 & =a(u-{u}_{1})(u-{u}_{2}) \\\\  & =(u-(2+6\\text{i}))(u-(2-6\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, among the given options, only $u-(2-6\\text{i})$ is a factor of ${u}^{2}-4u+40.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46657" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2f3b35cd8b358cc9172c7517507c82854978f7cf090f8872c2b39fc9fe496f7a"} {"question" "q-46657" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46657" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "u+(1+4\\text{i})"] ["math" "u-(-2-6\\text{i})"] ["math" "u-(1-4\\text{i})"] ["math" "u-(2-6\\text{i})"] ["math" "u-(3-4\\text{i})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46657" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "u-(2-6\\text{i})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quadratic polynomial $f(v)$ has real coefficients, has roots ${v}_{1}=3+4\\text{i}$ and ${v}_{2}=3-4\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $2.$ Find $f(v).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${v}_{1}=3+4\\text{i}$ and ${v}_{2}=3-4\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(v-{v}_{1})(v-{v}_{2}) & =2(v-(3+4\\text{i}))(v-(3-4\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(v-(3+4\\text{i}))(v-(3-4\\text{i})) & =2({v}^{2}-(3+4\\text{i})v-(3-4\\text{i})v+(3+4\\text{i})(3-4\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2({v}^{2}-(3+4\\text{i}+3-4\\text{i})v+({3}^{2}-{4}^{2}{\\text{i}}^{2})) \\\\  & =2({v}^{2}-6v+(9+16)) \\\\  & =2{v}^{2}-12v+50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(v)=2{v}^{2}-12v+50.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2f3b35cd8b358cc9172c7517507c82854978f7cf090f8872c2b39fc9fe496f7a"} {"question" "q-46669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{v}^{2}+6v+25"] ["math" "2{v}^{2}+8v-14"] ["math" "2{v}^{2}-12v+50"] ["math" "2{v}^{2}-16v-14"] ["math" "2{v}^{2}-6v+50"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-46669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{v}^{2}-12v+50"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-107519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quadratic polynomial $P(y)$ has the double root ${y}_{1}={y}_{2}=7,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-2.$ Find $P(y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-107519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root ${y}_{1}={y}_{2}=7,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(y-{y}_{1})^{2} & =(-2){(y-7)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2){(y-7)}^{2} & =(-2)({y}^{2}-14y+49) \\\\  & =-2{y}^{2}+28y-98.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(y)=-2{y}^{2}+28y-98.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-107519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2f3b35cd8b358cc9172c7517507c82854978f7cf090f8872c2b39fc9fe496f7a"} {"question" "q-107519" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-107519" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2{y}^{2}+21y+7"] ["math" "-2{y}^{2}+21y-7"] ["math" "-2{y}^{2}+28y-98"] ["math" "-2{y}^{2}-28y-98"] ["math" "{y}^{2}-14y+49"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"} {"question" "q-107519" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2{y}^{2}+28y-98"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990129/state.json" "file_sha256" "52c1cf7269129d1b2a02a6a6671a1d22726318649e35e8b2d1ca628fe8938ae1"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1014 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
